  "description": "CR 500.5a whole card: the animation outlives the step it was made in",
  "note": "alice animates her Jade Statue in the beginning of combat step, and it is still a 3/6 creature once that step has ended. This is the case a step-scoped duration fails: an implementation that ended the effect at the end of the step it was created in would leave a plain artifact in the declare attackers step, and would still pass a test that only asked whether it is a creature during combat and not next turn. Two Mountains, so the ability is activated once.",
